{\n        \"@type\": \"Question\",\n        \"name\": \"What are the 85 minerals in Shilajit?\",\n        \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n          \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n          \"text\": \"Shilajit contains over 85 minerals, including calcium, magnesium, zinc, potassium, copper, and iron, all of which are essential for the body’s health.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \n      {\n        \"@type\": \"Question\",\n        \"name\": \"Does Shilajit have magnesium?\",\n        \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n          \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n          \"text\": \"Yes, it contains magnesium, which supports muscle function, bone health, and energy production, with 20 to 30 mg per 100 grams.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \n      {\n        \"@type\": \"Question\",\n        \"name\": \"What are the active compounds in Shilajit?\",\n        \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n          \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n          \"text\": \"Active compounds include 7% fulvic acid, 10% humic acid, and 85+ trace minerals for accelerated nutrient absorption and support various bodily functions.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \n      {\n        \"@type\": \"Question\",\n        \"name\": \"Does Shilajit contain fulvic acid?\",\n        \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n          \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n          \"text\": \"Shilajit contains 7% fulvic acid.&nbsp;\"\n        }\n      },\n      \n      {\n        \"@type\": \"Question\",\n        \"name\": \"Is Shilajit a mineral or an herb?\",\n        \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n          \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n          \"text\": \"It’s a mineral-rich substance, not an herb, formed from decomposed plant matter and minerals over thousands of years.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \n      {\n        \"@type\": \"Question\",\n        \"name\": \"How is Shilajit purified?\",\n        \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n          \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n          \"text\": \"Shilajit is purified through a filtration process to remove impurities, toxins, and heavy metals, ensuring its safety for consumption.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \n      {\n        \"@type\": \"Question\",\n        \"name\": \"What is the difference between raw and purified Shilajit?\",\n        \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n          \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n          \"text\": \"Raw Shilajit may contain impurities and toxins, while purified Shilajit has undergone a cleaning process to ensure safety and potency.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \n      {\n        \"@type\": \"Question\",\n        \"name\": \"Does Shilajit contain heavy metals?\",\n        \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n          \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n          \"text\": \"High-quality Shilajit is purified to remove heavy metals. It’s essential to buy from trusted sources that test for purity and safety.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \n      {\n        \"@type\": \"Question\",\n        \"name\": \"Can I take Shilajit and Berberine together?\",\n        \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n          \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n          \"text\": \"Yes, they can be taken together. Both offer different health benefits, but it’s best to consult a healthcare professional before combining supplements.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \n      {\n        \"@type\": \"Question\",\n        \"name\": \"Can I take sea moss and Shilajit together?\",\n        \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n          \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n          \"text\": \"Yes, they can complement each other. Both support health, with sea moss providing iodine and Shilajit offering essential minerals.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \n      {\n        \"@type\": \"Question\",\n        \"name\": \"Which is better, Ashwagandha or Shilajit?\",\n        \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n          \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n          \"text\": \"Both supplements have their strengths. Ashwagandha is great for stress relief, while Shilajit boosts energy and vitality. They can be taken together for optimal results.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \n      {\n        \"@type\": \"Question\",\n        \"name\": \"Can you put Shilajit